WEBVTT

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:07.440
Oh, uh-huh.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:19.870
Nah, I've gotta get up.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:44.890
Ano ano donna iro ga ima desuka?

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:46.150
Egao no white

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:47.600
Namida no blue

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:50.230
Kasanete mita toki

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:55.570
Honjitsu seiten nari canvas ni

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:58.280
Milk no ice, ramune gokun

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:00.950
Genki ni color topping

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:05.000
Oi! ough gaki please

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:10.920
Minna no nigaoe contest

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:13.670
Yuno

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:18.180
Yoshi! Ato de ''pun'' okoranai de ne

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:16.930
Miyako

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:19.430
Hiro

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:25.270
Switch osaretara wa-ha-ha

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:22.680
Sae

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:31.610
Nanka ii kimochi nareba ii kanji

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:33.150
Kyousou da

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:35.940
Ichihayaku ringo tabeyo

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:38.530
Sou ja nainda yo

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:42.200
Sou de iinda yo

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:47.160
Kudamono wa model san

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:52.000
Saa dessin shimasho ka

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.880
Shukudai dayo

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:02.350
March 13, 3% of Hope

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:07.230
I'm such a lazy bum.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:10.690
I've gotta do it.

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:12.480
Time for news at noon.

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:27.120
Morning!

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:30.170
Good morning. Please, come in.

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:32.960
Oh, are you working on something, Yunocchi?

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:36.050
I wanted to draw something.

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:39.170
It's almost spring, right?

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:42.890
We started attending Yamabuki High
last spring.

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:46.520
I wanted to see how much I've improved.

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:47.850
I see.

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:51.230
But I don't even know what to start on.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:57.070
Today is a holiday, so I wanted to
focus on drawing this morning,

00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:59.030
but I just woke up a while ago.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.360
Same here, I woke up two minutes ago.

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:08.700
I'm disappointed. I actually haven't decided
what to draw; I keep wasting time.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.290
It might be because you don't
have any deadlines.

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:12.920
Maybe so.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:15.750
I want to draw something. Name a subject.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.550
Well, how about a cat?

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:21.680
It's got fangs?

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:23.720
This thing is strong.

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:26.970
These things, I can draw quickly.

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:31.890
How lovely.

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:33.440
Thanks.

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:35.060
What's next?

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:36.820
How about flowers?

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:38.400
Flower petals...

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:44.990
Loves me... loves me not...
loves me... loves me not...

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:46.280
Done!

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:47.660
Me too.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:49.620
That feels like spring.

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:52.790
You even added roots? They look so realistic.

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:54.420
Next is rice.

00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:57.290
Like this?

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:00.880
I need colors.

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:09.640
Oh, it's from Sae.

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:17.440
''If you're free, come over.
Use the window by the yard.''

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:19.520
Roger that!

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:22.110
I can fly!

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:23.740
Oh no, Miya!

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:26.780
A perfect 10.

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:28.410
Oh really?

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:32.450
The blue of the sky is so pretty.

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:35.210
So is the pink of your panties, Yunocchi.

00:04:43.130 --> 00:04:44.680
Ouch...

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:46.510
Yunocchi, well done.

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:48.550
I heard something.

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:50.970
Yahoo, we flew here.

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:53.140
Quite literally.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:56.020
You jumped from upstairs?

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:59.020
You should have come through
the backyard.

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:02.900
We're fine, but why from the back?

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:09.990
I'm pretending not to be home,
so I don't want anyone to use the door.

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:13.620
What's this? Are you hiding
from a debt collector?

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:15.250
I'm not you.

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:22.500
My deadlines are tight,
so I'm avoiding my editor.

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:26.550
You're a professional novelist, right?
That's awesome.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:31.180
It's not. The deadline has passed,
but my mind is blank.

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:33.100
Is that so?

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:34.730
I know!

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:37.230
Done!

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:39.900
Master Sae, I'll help you out of this pinch.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:43.110
Check out Miyako's special story cards!

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:45.150
I was wondering what you were doing.

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:50.660
Who will do what and where?

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:56.120
You draw cards at random,
and you get a story in no time.

00:05:56.410 --> 00:05:57.910
Here you go!

00:05:57.910 --> 00:05:59.420
A monk...

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:00.920
...on the plains...

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:02.420
...saury fish...

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:03.590
...steam...

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:06.090
A monk steamed a saury on the plains.

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:09.130
Why don't you write that story?

00:06:09.130 --> 00:06:10.800
A saury on the plains?

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:14.850
Hey, I'm focusing on using real life events.

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:16.140
I see.

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:20.770
I don't think I can write a realistic novel
unless it's based on my own experiences.

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:22.650
You're amazing, Sae.

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:25.610
That's something I always keep in mind.

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:31.240
Well then, you can't write a romance,
can you? You have no experience.

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:33.910
How rude!

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:38.040
Yes, she does. You seem to have
lots of romantic experiences.

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:47.630
Yeah, when I was in junior high, I had eight
boyfriends, so I had to switch each day.

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:52.220
So, why did you call us?

00:06:52.590 --> 00:06:54.930
Berry Mart

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:55.350
Welcome.

00:06:55.350 --> 00:07:00.690
All right, I'll go get the energy drinks,
so you get the dried squid.

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:02.980
Roger that.

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:02.980
Appetizers

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:02.980
For a Fun Party

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:02.980
For Children's Snacks

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:09.110
I wonder which one she likes?
Berry Mart has so many appetizers.

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:12.240
Miya!

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:17.200
What do you think? It a cute squid-kun.

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:20.120
That ''kun'' probably means jerky, actually.

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:24.290
Thank you very much.

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:30.670
A total of 945 yen. Sae must have known
before handing us out a 1000 yen bill.

00:07:31.510 --> 00:07:33.970
New Release Corner

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:34.800
What's wrong?

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:38.390
It's Aya Tachibana.

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:39.520
Really?

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:41.310
Yeah, I saw it in her room just a while ago.

00:07:42.390 --> 00:07:44.900
Look! So is this Sae?

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:48.400
Monthly Kirara

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:47.320
Her name is on the cover.

00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:48.940
Where is it?

00:07:49.190 --> 00:07:52.280
Umm, page 98.

00:07:52.650 --> 00:07:54.450
Yunocchi, a bit before that.

00:07:57.660 --> 00:08:00.580
''Yuka didn't see her sister leaving.''

00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:07.170
''She didn't want to accept the fact that
her sister was moving away.''

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:15.800
''Mika was nervous because of mixed emotions
of wanting and not wanting to see Yuka.''

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:19.810
''The day Yuka specified finally came.''

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:24.850
''Since the morning, Mika had been nervous
because of the mixed emotions of wanting...''

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:29.400
''And so Mika and Yuka parted ways.''

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:33.450
Wow!

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:35.240
Wait, don't tell me yet.

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:39.740
Oh, Hiro.

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:41.580
Goodness...

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:43.210
Shopping?

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:45.580
Wow, you bought a lot of stuff.

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:48.340
Yeah, I'll fix some nighttime snacks for Sae.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:51.670
I always make something before her deadlines.

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:55.130
I want her to eat well,
especially when things are tough.

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:57.220
Hiro, I have a deadline too.

00:08:57.220 --> 00:09:01.810
Miya, don't. Sae is working really hard.

00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:06.560
Hiro, why is Sae attending the art
department of the Yamabuki High

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:10.020
even though she already has a writing job?

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:13.820
I guess I can tell you guys.

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:19.200
Sae wants to draw the insert illustrations
for her novels on her own.

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:24.580
She says only she can draw illustrations
that truly match her ideas.

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:27.830
Wow, Sae is great.

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:30.880
What an incredible publicity stunt.

00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:34.010
You are using the idiom wrong.

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:36.380
We're back!

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:37.930
Huh?

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:39.550
Quiet.

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:43.680
She seems to be on a roll,
so let's leave quietly.

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:45.520
Okay.

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:47.310
I'll leave the stuff here.

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:51.730
Curry that has set overnight
tastes the best.

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:56.360
I feel kind of bad.

00:09:56.440 --> 00:09:57.490
For what?

00:09:57.490 --> 00:10:04.200
Well, because we're eating together while
Sae is working so hard in the next room.

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:09.290
Yes, but she doesn't want to eat
anything while in the groove.

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:12.130
She forgets about hunger.

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:14.130
A novel-writing diet?

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:16.170
Hiro, perhaps you should write too.

00:10:16.170 --> 00:10:20.890
It's pointless because once she's done,
she'll end up eating a lot to make up.

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:24.100
That doesn't sound healthy, does it?

00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:29.140
True, I wish she'd eat properly.

00:10:29.140 --> 00:10:33.770
I'll fix something that she can
eat while working, but...

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:38.400
Like rice balls, sandwiches and
dried persimmons...

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:44.030
I heard that there was an earl who
was really into card games,

00:10:44.030 --> 00:10:48.870
and the sandwich was invented so
he could eat while playing.

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:56.090
So, the ''sandwich'' was named after the
earl whose name was Sandwich.

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:57.460
Did you know that?

00:10:57.460 --> 00:10:58.800
Of course!

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:01.970
Sae doesn't eat it, either?

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:06.140
I guess I began to adapt to
her circumstances.

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:10.350
Her schedule becomes irregular
before every deadline.

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:13.730
Sometimes Sae doesn't even sleep.

00:11:14.730 --> 00:11:17.230
She also takes energy drinks, right?

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:21.530
If she's like that at her age, I can't
help but worry about her future.

00:11:22.450 --> 00:11:26.410
She becomes rather touchy
when she gets stuck.

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:28.950
Haven't you seen her like that?

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:30.750
No.

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:36.250
Whenever she acts like that, I try to be
quiet even when I bring her food.

00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:38.380
Even I get nervous because of that.

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:41.380
So, when I get back to my place I
just sit down and do nothing.

00:11:43.050 --> 00:11:46.680
I guess having a deadline is very stressful.

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:49.970
I don't know if I could be like Hiro.

00:11:57.900 --> 00:11:59.400
March 13

00:11:57.900 --> 00:11:59.400
School Holiday Announcement

00:11:57.900 --> 00:11:59.400
<i>Today, March 13, is a substitute holiday
for the class that was held...</i>

00:12:13.370 --> 00:12:15.000
Safe.

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:21.050
I must do it.

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:28.930
Hello!

00:12:29.180 --> 00:12:30.560
Hi, Miya.

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:32.680
Cover your knees with this.

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:34.140
Thank you.

00:12:34.140 --> 00:12:35.770
Sorry to bother you.

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:40.570
It's nice of you to be with me, but you
don't have to. It's still cool outside.

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:42.650
I have my own blanket.

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:45.990
This feels so warm.

00:12:46.450 --> 00:12:47.820
Berry Mart

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:49.910
Look.

00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:51.910
The principal...

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:54.500
Even though the school is closed, he's here.

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:56.330
He bought some food?

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:58.960
Looks like it, but why green onions?

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:01.920
So, the principal can cook.

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:04.170
What? At school?

00:13:04.300 --> 00:13:05.970
He can use the home economics room.

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:12.720
But why does the principal have to
cook at school on a holiday?

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:16.190
Could it be that the principal...

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:18.150
...lives on campus?

00:13:18.270 --> 00:13:18.900
Utility Gate

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:24.780
Just like him. It's exactly what you'd
expect from the principal.

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:28.700
So, the principal really likes Yamabuki High.

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:31.620
Mathematics
Trisection of an Angle,
Squaring the Circle

00:13:29.990 --> 00:13:31.660
You're studying math?

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:34.790
Yup! You're working so hard, so I will too.

00:13:36.410 --> 00:13:38.370
Don't you like to do that inside?

00:13:38.370 --> 00:13:40.380
I'll fall asleep if I do that.

00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:41.710
I see.

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:45.050
They say, ''In spring, he who is
sleeping knows no dawn.''

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:50.470
Come and get me, math. Come and get me.

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:54.220
Something's not right.
Do you think this is okay?

00:13:54.220 --> 00:13:55.350
What?

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:56.980
Good!

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:09.570
Do you want some tea?

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:10.700
I'll have it.

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:12.370
I have snacks too.

00:14:18.830 --> 00:14:35.100
''I slept too long and have a headache (> < ) I
feel dizzy and haven't done much lately...
I want to go to karaoke with Yuno and Miyako.
Who's your favorite singer~?''

00:14:19.580 --> 00:14:22.920
''I slept too long and have a headache.''

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:27.420
'I feel dizzy and haven't done much lately...''

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:31.760
''I want to go to karaoke with Yuno and Miyako.''

00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:35.100
''Who's your favorite singer~?''

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:35.390
''Who's your favorite singer~?''

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:38.270
Sounds good. I want to go to karaoke.

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:45.110
''Let's! The Mermaid is my favorite.''

00:14:45.110 --> 00:14:46.610
Is this good?

00:14:46.610 --> 00:14:48.740
Tell her to read the Monthly Kirara.

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:49.900
- Sent -

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:54.660
Hello.

00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:55.830
Lo!

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:58.450
Hello, Yuno, Miyako.

00:14:58.870 --> 00:15:02.040
Do you have work on a school holiday?

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:05.000
No, I came to have some fun.

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:08.800
You must like Yamabuki High too.

00:15:09.090 --> 00:15:11.590
I didn't have a choice,

00:15:11.590 --> 00:15:16.930
because my parents nagged at me for
staying home and doing nothing.

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:19.850
I didn't do anything because it's a holiday!

00:15:20.140 --> 00:15:22.150
You were kicked out of your place?

00:15:22.150 --> 00:15:26.320
No! I left the house!

00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:29.240
I won't forgive them even if they apologize.

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:38.660
Even though it's a holiday,
I'll offer you a special class.

00:15:47.590 --> 00:15:52.090
Tell me where I should be,
and decide my pose.

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:57.180
Oh, if you can wait for a bit,
I can go get my costume.

00:15:57.640 --> 00:16:01.350
Ms. Yoshinoya, you just left
your home, didn't you?

00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:04.730
I'll sneak in and get one, if it's for Yuno.

00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:09.480
Oh, look.

00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:14.320
What is he carrying?

00:16:15.110 --> 00:16:16.370
It's soy sauce.

00:16:16.370 --> 00:16:19.370
He must have forgotten to buy some.

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:22.660
He didn't buy anything else,
so he didn't get a plastic bag.

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:25.460
The principal must be eco-conscious.

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:29.250
But when did he come out?

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:30.760
He must have used warp speed.

00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:32.380
What?

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:34.800
I didn't know the principal was here.

00:16:34.970 --> 00:16:37.550
Actually, the principal lives on campus.

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:50.020
Hey, what should I do if something
like that happens again.

00:16:50.230 --> 00:16:51.570
You didn't want to draw her?

00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:57.950
I don't mind doing it,
but it doesn't quite match my motivation.

00:16:58.070 --> 00:17:00.200
Maybe you can just pretend?

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:03.040
She'll figure it out right away.

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:06.540
How about, ''Maybe the next time?''

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:09.250
I wonder if she'd accept that?

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:15.880
I wonder how adults would respond
to this kind of situation?

00:17:17.140 --> 00:17:18.970
What does it mean to be an adult?

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:20.970
What is it, really?

00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:26.730
Shall we continue?

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:28.770
Sure.

00:17:34.150 --> 00:17:35.780
Hiro...

00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:38.910
Welcome back.

00:17:38.910 --> 00:17:40.580
How is Sae doing?

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:42.200
Dunno.

00:17:44.450 --> 00:17:46.040
Goodness...

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:51.840
Miya, there's a blanket in the closet.
Can you get it?

00:17:51.840 --> 00:17:53.050
Sure.

00:17:53.050 --> 00:17:55.510
Did she finish her novel?

00:17:56.760 --> 00:18:00.550
''I only have the last scene to go,
then I'll get some sleep.''

00:18:04.560 --> 00:18:06.350
Don't you have a headache?

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:12.820
Here you go, Hiro.

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:15.320
Huh?

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:22.950
All right, it's done.

00:18:23.450 --> 00:18:25.080
Right here.

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:30.330
Do I have to?

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:32.040
Yunocchi, fly!

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:34.090
You're okay, right, Miya?

00:18:34.090 --> 00:18:35.550
No scratches.

00:18:35.550 --> 00:18:40.590
No way... It's impossible!
I'm scared! I'm so scared!

00:18:40.590 --> 00:18:42.220
Yunocchi, fly!

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:45.350
Go!

00:18:45.520 --> 00:18:46.270
Oh, no! Please help!

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:46.930
It's only 1 .5 meters or so to the ground.
Oh, no! Please help!

00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:48.850
It's only 1 .5 meters or so to the ground.

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:50.480
You'll be fine.

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:52.310
No, I can't.

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:55.980
I must have looked so stupid.

00:18:56.860 --> 00:19:01.320
But Sae didn't see me, and Hiro wasn't there.

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:04.280
I hope Miya forgets about it.

00:19:08.410 --> 00:19:10.080
Cheers!

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:10.920
We don't have to...

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:15.670
Why not? There's nothing wrong
celebrating your success.

00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:18.630
Success, I guess so, but...

00:19:19.470 --> 00:19:20.970
Congratulations.

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:22.510
Thank you.

00:19:22.510 --> 00:19:25.430
When will today's episode be published?

00:19:25.430 --> 00:19:27.310
Maybe next month.

00:19:27.640 --> 00:19:30.230
Miya, when it comes out, let's go read it again.

00:19:30.230 --> 00:19:31.310
Sure thing!

00:19:31.310 --> 00:19:33.270
Did you just say ''again?''

00:19:33.650 --> 00:19:37.110
Oh, I went to a bookstore
with Miya earlier today.

00:19:37.110 --> 00:19:40.240
It was about sisters.

00:19:41.400 --> 00:19:44.410
How did you know? I didn't
tell you my pen name.

00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:48.200
You honestly thought you'd be
able to hide it from me?

00:19:48.910 --> 00:19:55.170
I think it's okay. I personally want
more people to know about your book.

00:19:55.630 --> 00:19:58.380
This episode was fun, too.

00:19:59.130 --> 00:20:00.460
Really?

00:20:00.460 --> 00:20:07.050
Yeah... It's about Kensuke and Nanami,
who live in the same apartment building.

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:12.390
They were friends since they were young,
but when they enter high school,

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:14.190
they begin to see each other
as more than just friends.

00:20:14.190 --> 00:20:16.940
No, no, no, no, no! Hiro, don't!

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:20.780
What's wrong? Once it's published,
anyone can read it.

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:23.780
True, but I just don't like it.

00:20:25.280 --> 00:20:28.910
You know the last scene, when they confess
their feelings? I got so excited.

00:20:28.910 --> 00:20:30.660
Enough already.

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:34.750
Is it based on your own experience too?

00:20:35.420 --> 00:20:40.170
Yeah, of course. I've done it as many
times as there are stars in the sky.

00:20:40.550 --> 00:20:42.630
You have a large stock of stories to tell.

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:44.930
Yup, some billions.

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:54.060
Hiro and Sae are great friends.
They know and trust each other.

00:20:55.100 --> 00:20:58.770
I wonder if you and I can become like that?

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:06.910
I'm always looking for someone
who will cook for me.

00:21:07.780 --> 00:21:09.240
That's not what I meant.

00:21:09.620 --> 00:21:14.790
Sorry, Miya, I forgot about a package
I accepted for you.

00:21:14.790 --> 00:21:16.460
Will you come down and get it?

00:21:16.460 --> 00:21:18.080
Okay!

00:21:19.500 --> 00:21:20.500
What is it?

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:22.550
It's really heavy. I wonder what's inside?

00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:24.880
Hokkai Seafood

00:21:22.630 --> 00:21:24.090
The delight of the Hokkai Sea...

00:21:24.090 --> 00:21:25.680
Could it be...

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:27.260
Wow!

00:21:28.140 --> 00:21:30.640
I entered a sweepstake a while ago.

00:21:30.930 --> 00:21:32.680
You won, Miya!

00:21:32.770 --> 00:21:34.640
That's awesome. Congratulations.

00:21:38.650 --> 00:21:41.150
Oh, my beautiful delights from the Hokkai Sea.

00:21:46.110 --> 00:21:52.490
Miya and I are already great friends
just like Hiro and Sae.

00:21:53.790 --> 00:21:59.080
I was able to finish my painting
because Miya was with me.

00:22:06.300 --> 00:22:08.680
<i>The end of March 13
To Be Continued</i>

